                                                "example_id": "aa802be9-af54-4e98-b676-e57ba86a774c",
                                                "sense_id": "3823d4dc-4902-30a7-8c31-fa08d5f6fe70",
                                                "text": "The government here is corrupt, so we'll emigrate to escape them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae5d0b6d-9413-4642-a00e-c54ef4adb49d",
                                                "sense_id": "3823d4dc-4902-30a7-8c31-fa08d5f6fe70",
                                                "text": "The earth also was corrupt before God, and the earth was filled with violence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5e2d250-38ec-446d-a0ae-483419ea49d5",
                                                "sense_id": "3823d4dc-4902-30a7-8c31-fa08d5f6fe70",
                                                "text": "At what ease\nMight corrupt minds procure knaves as corrupt\nTo swear against you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fde7835e-bd7f-3b49-9b96-93a1c07de3f3",
                                        "entry_id": "45eec8ca-0e81-30fe-9d79-b31343bb1866",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Abounding in errors; not genuine or correct; in an invalid state."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e96aed5-1959-4d08-bee2-a4ec6dce4b0a",
                                                "sense_id": "fde7835e-bd7f-3b49-9b96-93a1c07de3f3",
                                                "text": "The text of the manuscript is corrupt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fedc551d-ae2b-4c7b-8b06-9f3a86386251",
                                                "sense_id": "fde7835e-bd7f-3b49-9b96-93a1c07de3f3",
                                                "text": "It turned out that the program was corrupt - that's why it wouldn't open."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ebf996a9-63d3-31f0-809c-5bad8799d576",
                                        "entry_id": "45eec8ca-0e81-30fe-9d79-b31343bb1866",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a putrid state; spoiled; tainted; vitiated; unsound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eeb22a23-39f5-44ef-9d37-db77f63931e3",
                                                "sense_id": "ebf996a9-63d3-31f0-809c-5bad8799d576",
                                                "text": "with such corrupt and pestilent bread to feed them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "corrupt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a826cadd-d953-3441-a95a-797777ca5328",
                                        "entry_id": "80f74680-8b9e-3a77-b2c4-291258101eb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make corrupt; to change from good to bad; to draw away from the right path; to deprave; to pervert."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "049fbc83-43db-49d3-998a-021f8150a958",
                                                "sense_id": "a826cadd-d953-3441-a95a-797777ca5328",
                                                "text": "Don't you dare corrupt my son with those disgusting pictures!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68006a34-b6b2-4ae6-b6f7-292a4d68b58f",
                                                "sense_id": "a826cadd-d953-3441-a95a-797777ca5328",
                                                "text": "And God looked upon the earth, and, behold, it was corrupt; for all flesh had corrupted his way upon the earth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f068b19a-0a41-41f9-9387-05457b335ebc",
                                                "sense_id": "a826cadd-d953-3441-a95a-797777ca5328",
                                                "text": "I think that there is a bad idea around in our world, and that idea is that 'power corrupts, and absolute power corrupts absolutely'. I think what really happens is that power attracts the corruptible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2605b0d6-c711-43ae-90b4-b6aa323d8092",
                                                "sense_id": "a826cadd-d953-3441-a95a-797777ca5328",
                                                "text": "George Soros remains a favorite target of conservative conspiracy theorists, seeing his corrupting influence behind every liberal movement and within every nook and cranny."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63700273-6fe8-3c17-9e4a-e419708f5be5",
                                        "entry_id": "80f74680-8b9e-3a77-b2c4-291258101eb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become putrid, tainted, or otherwise impure; to putrefy; to rot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2220b18-a517-452d-b79e-7f27a6c0c50c",
                                                "sense_id": "63700273-6fe8-3c17-9e4a-e419708f5be5",
                                                "text": "he entrails, which are the parts aptest to corrupt"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6385742-115d-46ad-9ec9-ad9342596868",
                                                "sense_id": "63700273-6fe8-3c17-9e4a-e419708f5be5",
                                                "text": "[…] Lanfrank takes Notice of Tract. 3. Doct. 3. cap. 18. ſaying, \"I have ſeen many who being full of Humours, have made an Iſſue under the Knee, before due Purgation had been premis'd; whence, by reaſon of the too great Defluxion of Humours, the Legs tumified, ſo that the cauterized Place corrupted, and a Cancer (or rather cacoethic Ulcer) was thereby made, with which great Difficulty was cur'd.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "687416fd-73b8-3fe6-b221-1af91cc41929",
                                        "entry_id": "80f74680-8b9e-3a77-b2c4-291258101eb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To introduce errors; to place into an invalid state."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "782597ac-9ad8-4750-9d4d-2fef8e9cfb82",
                                                "sense_id": "687416fd-73b8-3fe6-b221-1af91cc41929",
                                                "text": "Unplugging a flash drive without dismounting it first can corrupt the data stored on the drive."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2cf90c9-a1f0-3275-8d42-98be50b3cf6f",
                                        "entry_id": "80f74680-8b9e-3a77-b2c4-291258101eb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To debase or make impure by alterations or additions; to falsify."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "432ccf84-7057-4fc4-b2ab-bde800ae669f",
                                                "sense_id": "f2cf90c9-a1f0-3275-8d42-98be50b3cf6f",
                                                "text": "to corrupt language, or a holy text"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e9b7d29-4c29-4686-ab39-db590b3b9a22",
                                                "sense_id": "f2cf90c9-a1f0-3275-8d42-98be50b3cf6f",
                                                "text": "to corrupt a book"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d83d8b4-d857-3a90-8686-8f891787c48e",
                                        "entry_id": "80f74680-8b9e-3a77-b2c4-291258101eb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To waste, spoil, or consume; to make worthless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40445daa-c753-4a87-b701-df1f8c73a76c",
                                                "sense_id": "0d83d8b4-d857-3a90-8686-8f891787c48e",
                                                "text": "Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c2343278-b508-48d7-9cdb-73a072dfee1f",
                        "source_entry_id": "f4973b0e-30d3-36f8-86e8-80835c0d7c82",
                        "source_sense_id": "b3708dba-04da-3b04-b2ee-9410393b2c96",
                        "target_lang_word": "dépravé",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dépravé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fc55716-cabc-3def-aad7-abd2fd9ccc69",
                                        "entry_id": "b86f6d0d-9200-3b78-bc1b-7c4d84872640",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui vit dans la dépravation, dans la débauche, dans le vice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ad68fca-3190-4920-a157-1a236263a662",
                                                "sense_id": "3fc55716-cabc-3def-aad7-abd2fd9ccc69",
                                                "text": "Elle n’était pas dépravée ; sa passion, au contraire, se montrait robuste et saine, et, dans ses embrassements, elle avait la noblesse terrible, l’héroïsme rugissant des grands fauves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f803fbd0-6dab-4918-bf7e-359434a708b0",
                                                "sense_id": "3fc55716-cabc-3def-aad7-abd2fd9ccc69",
                                                "text": "Dans le nombre de ces Parisiens accusés d’être si spirituels, il s’en trouve qui se croient infiniment mieux en uniforme que dans leurs habits ordinaires, et qui supposent chez les femmes des goûts assez dépravés pour imaginer qu’elles seront favorablement impressionnées à l’aspect d’un bonnet à poil et par le harnais militaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb938e1c-1b99-4e76-bf0d-45fcd16419c1",
                                                "sense_id": "3fc55716-cabc-3def-aad7-abd2fd9ccc69",
                                                "text": "Carel me parla d'une querelle entre eux, Rembrandt me traitant de prostituée, de soiffarde dépravée, alors Carel l'a frappé. Il l'a frappé... Pour moi."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dépravé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2af6391b-9f83-34f3-a0cc-4cae1560992d",
                                        "entry_id": "c131b573-d632-3e82-ae9f-0f28024640c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Participe passé masculin singulier de dépraver."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36f9cea0-c1c7-4469-b36e-b55d94726dbc",
                                                "sense_id": "2af6391b-9f83-34f3-a0cc-4cae1560992d",
                                                "text": "Moins surveillé par David à Angoulême, soit que plus âgé il inspirât plus de confiance à son mentor, soit que l’imprimeur comptât sur l’influence de la province, Cérizet était devenu, mais à l’insu de son tuteur, le don Juan en casquette de trois ou quatre petites ouvrières, et s’était dépravé complètement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "9bb7126b-38f5-3aa8-ae5a-098198b4659d",
                "word": "verdorven",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bf2620ed-fa13-341e-b6bc-d4589ec62578",
                        "entry_id": "9bb7126b-38f5-3aa8-ae5a-098198b4659d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "voltooid deelwoord van verderven"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "905185c1-cb2c-4949-b874-b7f6f7a29db4",
                                "sense_id": "bf2620ed-fa13-341e-b6bc-d4589ec62578",
                                "text": "En hebben hun goden in het vuur geworpen; want zij waren geen goden, maar het werk van mensenhanden, hout en steen; daarom hebben zij die verdorven."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
